<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25194" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jānĭtor</span></b>  (‡ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jānĭtos</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 27</span></i>
		Müll.), ōris, m.
		janua, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a door-keeper, porter, janitor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">heus ecquis hic est janitor? aperite,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Men. 4, 2, 110</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carceris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 45, § 118</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">janitor (indignum!) durā religate
					catenā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 1, 6, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">utque sedens vester primi prope limina tecti,
					janitor egressus videt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					1, 138</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2, 7, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. C. 3,
				14, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tib. 1, 1, 65</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 1
				praef.</span></i>— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b>, transf. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Caeli janitor, i. e. <i>Janus</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. F.
				1, 139</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> (Ingens) janitor, of <i>Cerberus</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 6,
				400</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3, 11, 16</span></i>.</div>
